  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-07-22T18:36:13.020Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Allow for an optional feature within the SDK for a button that generates a texture atlas for all textures on an avatar. Have a method that crams textures on a grid that creates a texture atlas. For example, if there are 4 textures, it can be reduced to one large texture atlas. If there are 12 textures, it can reduce to three large texture atlases. If there are 30, it can reduce to eight large texture atlases. If there is an insane 100 textures, it can be reduce to 25 texture atlases. Allowing textures to be consolidated into divisions (perhaps four to eight textures to one atlas), it can reduce the amount of draw calls significantly and greatly optimize the game with the click of a button. I suggest this button to be placed in the VRChat SDK’s Unity tab and kept optional in case there are shader or texture quality issues or if such optimization is unnecessary.",
